          %title Contents
          %blockquote
            %p under construction
            %p
              for the time being this here are nothing but
              %a{:href => "#References"} references
              and rough notes taken in a talk long ago…
          %p
            %em BDR 2-vector bundles
            are a notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorified"} categorified
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            motivated by the concept of
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/2-vector+space#KV2VectorSpace"} Kapranov-Voevodsy’s 2-vector spaces
          %p
            See also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/iterated+algebraic+K-theory"} iterated algebraic K-theory
          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#2vector_bundles_following_baasdundasrognes"} 2-Vector bundles following Baas-Dundas-Rognes
              %li
                %a{:href => "#the_homotopy_type_of_the_classifying_space"} The homotopy type of the classifying space
              %li
                %a{:href => "#_as_a_form_of_elliptic_cohomology"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ku
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(ku)
                  as a form of elliptic cohomology
              %li
                %a{:href => "#from_gerbes_to_2vector_bundles"} From gerbes to 2-vector bundles
              %li
                %a{:href => "#2K-theory"} 2K-theory of bimonoidal categories
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#References"} References
          %h2#2vector_bundles_following_baasdundasrognes 2-Vector bundles following Baas-Dundas-Rognes
          %p
            We are looking for a generalization of the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi α
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_\alpha \to X\}_{\alpha \in A}
            an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is assumed to be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
          %p
            Defition. A
            %strong charted 2-vector bundle
            (i.e. a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            for a BDR 2-vector bundle) of rank
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            is
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi β
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \lt \beta \in A
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi α
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi β
                      %mo =
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mrow
                          %mi α
                          %mi β
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_\alpha \cap U_\beta =: U_{\alpha\beta}
                a matrix
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi E
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                        %mrow
                          %mi α
                          %mi β
                      %msubsup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ,
                          %mi j
                          %mo =
                          %mn 1
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E^{\alpha\beta}_{i j})_{i,j = 1}^{n}
                of
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi E
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                        %mrow
                          %mi α
                          %mi β
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mrow
                          %mi α
                          %mi β
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^{\alpha \beta}_{i j} \to U_{\alpha \beta}
                such that the determinant of the underlying matrix of dimensions is
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi det
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi dim
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msubsup
                          %mi E
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                          %mrow
                            %mi α
                            %mi β
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mo ±
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} det(dim(E^{\alpha \beta}_{i j})) = \pm 1
            %li
              %p
                on triple overlaps
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mrow
                          %mi α
                          %mi β
                          %mi γ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{\alpha \beta \gamma}
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi β
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi γ
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \lt \beta \lt \gamma \in A
                we have
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mrow
                          %mi α
                          %mi β
                          %mi γ
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊕
                        %mi j
                      %msubsup
                        %mi E
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                        %mrow
                          %mi α
                          %mi β
                      %mo ⊗
                      %msubsup
                        %mi E
                        %mrow
                          %mi j
                          %mi k
                        %mrow
                          %mi β
                          %mi γ
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo ≃
                      %msubsup
                        %mi E
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi k
                        %mrow
                          %mi α
                          %mi γ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\phi^{\alpha \beta \gamma}
                      \:
                      \\oplus_{j} E^{\alpha \beta}_{i j} \otimes E^{\beta \gamma}_{j k}
                      \\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                      E^{\alpha \gamma}_{i k}
            %li
              %p
                such that the
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
                satisfy on quadruple overlaps the evident cocycle condition (as described at
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gerbe"} gerbe
                and
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundle"} principal 2-bundle
          %p Next we need to define morphisms of such charted 2-vector bundles. These involve the evident refinements of covers and fiberwise transformations.
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                  %mi Vect
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2Vect(X)
            for the equivalence classes of charted 2-vector bundles under these morphisms.
          %p
            %strong Remark
            If we restrict attention to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1
            then this gives the same as
            = succeed "-gerbes/" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbe"} bundle gerbe
          %p
            %strong Theorem
            (Baas-Dundas-Rognes)
          %p
            There exists a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{K}(V)
            such that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a finite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
            there is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝒦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mi lim
                        %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi Y
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                  %mi Gr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mi Vect
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [X, \mathcal{K}(V)] =
                  {\lim_\to}_{a : Y \to X}
                  Gr(2Vect(Y))
          %p
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            classes of continuous maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \mathcal{K}(V)
            and equivalence classes of the group completed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-stackification"} stackification
            of 2-vector bundles,
          %p
            where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            is over acyclic
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+fibration"} Serre fibration
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology"} homology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Gr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gr(-)
            indicates the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+group"} Grothendieck group
            completion using the monoid structure arising from the direct sum of 2-vector bundles.
          %p
            %strong Proof
            In BDR, Segal Birthday Proceedings
          %p
            %strong Note
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi Vect
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi Gl
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2Vect_n(X) = [X, |B Gl_n (V)| ]
          %p
            BDR called
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{K}(V)
            the
            %strong 2-K-theory
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bimonoidal+category"} bimonoidal category
            of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kapranov-Voevodsky+2-vector+space"} Kapranov-Voevodsky 2-vector space
          %h2#the_homotopy_type_of_the_classifying_space The homotopy type of the classifying space
          %p
            %strong Theorem
            (Baas-Dundas-Rognes-Richter)
          %p
            The K-theory of BDR 2-vector bundles is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ku"} ku
            (see at
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/iterated+algebraic+K-theory"} iterated algebraic K-theory
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ku
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{K}(V) \simeq K(ku)
          %p Here:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ku
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ku
                is the connected version of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
                of complex
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(-)
                denotes forming the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
                spectrum of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectrum"} ring spectra
          %p
            So by the general formula for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectrum"} ring spectra
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ku
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ×
                  %mi B
                  %mi Gl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ku
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  K(ku) \simeq \mathbb{Z} \times B Gl(ku)^+
                  \\,
          %p
            Some flavor of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{K}(V)
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                is the (a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skeleton"} skeleton
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
                of) of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                of complex
                = succeed "s." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"}> object
                    s are
                    = succeed "s," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                    corresponding to
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi ℂ
                              %mi n
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}^n
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"}> morphism
                    s are
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Hom
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi k
                          %mo ,
                          %mi k
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi GL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi k
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(k,k)  = GL(k)
                    and there are no morphisms between different
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo ,
                          %mi l
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k,l
                    \.
          %p
            This category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is naturally a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bimonoidal+category"} bimonoidal category
            under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
          %p
            K-theory is about understanding linear algebra on a ring, so we want to understand the linear algebra of this
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
          %p
            We write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Mat
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mat_n(V)
            for the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ×
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \times n
            matrices of linear isomorphisms between finite dimensional vector spaces.
          %p
            Such matrices can be multiplied using the usual formula for matrix products on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            of vector space and linear maps.
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Gl
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gl_n(V)
            for the subcollection of those matrices for which the determinant of their matrix of dimensions is
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ±
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pm 1
          %p Now define
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi Ω
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi Gl
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{K}(V) = \Omega B (\coprod_{n \geq 0} B Gl_n (V))
                  \\,.
          %p
            Notice that this is a direct generalization of the corresponding formula for the algebraic K-theory of a ring
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi Ω
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi Gl
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  K(R) = \Omega B (\coprod_{n \geq 0} B Gl_n(R))
                  \\,.
          %h2#_as_a_form_of_elliptic_cohomology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ku
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(ku)
            as a form of elliptic cohomology
          %p
            Ausoni and Rognes compute the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology"} homology
            groups (for a certain sense of homology) of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ku
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(ku)
          %p take rational homotopy
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi H
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℚ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^*(-, \mathbb{Q})
              %p
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime"} prime
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                gives an isomorphism on this.
              %p
                p =
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ν
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu_0
            %li
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi KU
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} KU^*(-)
                be complex oriented
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi KU
                        %mo *
                      %mo =
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi u
                        %mrow
                          %mo ±
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      KU_* = \mathbb{Z}[u^{\pm 1}]
              %p
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo =
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |u| = 2
                (the
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bott+class"} Bott class
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi u
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
                is an isomorphism and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi u
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi ν
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u^{p-1} = \nu_1
          %p
            The
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ν
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu_i
            come from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown-Peterson+spectrum"} Brown-Peterson spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B P
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo *
                  %mi BP
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi ν
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ν
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_* BP = \mathbb{Z}_{(p)}[\nu_1, \nu_2, \cdots]
          %p
            motto: the higher the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ν
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu_i
            the more you detect.
          %p Christian Ausoni figured out something that implies that
          %p
            “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ku
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(ku)
            detects as much in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
            as any other form of
            = succeed ".\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+cohomology"} elliptic cohomology
          %h2#from_gerbes_to_2vector_bundles From gerbes to 2-vector bundles
          %p
            It is hard to directly construct charted 2-vector bundles. We have more examples of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gerbe"} gerbe
          %p
            %strong Example
            We have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo =
                  %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{S}^1 = \mathbb{C}P^1 \subset \mathbb{C}P^\infty = B U(1) = K(\mathbb{Z},2)
          %p
            (see
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+space"} Eilenberg-MacLane space
            and
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %mn 3
                  %mo =
                  %mi Σ
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %mi Σ
                  %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi Σ
                  %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊗
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi units
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ku
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ku
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{S}^3 = \Sigma \mathbb{S}^2 \to \Sigma B U(1) \subset
                  \\Sigma B U \to B B U_{\otimes}
                  \\subset units(ku)
                  \\to B GL(ku)
          %p
            using
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mi BU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊗
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma B U(1) \to B BU(1) \to B B U_{\otimes}
            we can take a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gerbe"} gerbe
            classified by maps into
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^2 U(1)
            and induce from it the associated 2-vector bundle.
          %p the canonical map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %mn 3
                  %mo →
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{S}^3 \to K(\mathbb{Z},3)
          %p
            may be thought of as classifying the gerbe called the
            = succeed "-gerbe" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magnetic+monopole"} magnetic monopole
          %p
            Postcomposing with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                  %mo :
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ku
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu : K(\mathbb{Z},3) \to K(ku)
            we have
          %p
            Fact:
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
            gives a generator in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 3
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_3 K(\mathbb{Z},3) = H^3(\mathbb{S}^3)
          %p
            %strong Theorem
            (Ausoni-Dundas-Rognes)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi μ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                  %mi ζ
                  %mo −
                  %mi ν
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  j(\mu) = 2 \zeta - \nu
          %p
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ku
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_3(K(ku))
          %p
            so regarded as a 2-vector bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
            is not a generator.
          %p
            ADR:
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ζ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \zeta
            is “half a monopole”.
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ku
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 24
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi_3(K(ku))  = \mathbb{Z} \oplus \mathbb{Z}/24 \mathbb{Z}
          %p
            (the first summand is
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ζ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \zeta
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu
          %p
            Thomas Krogh has an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} orientation
            theory for 2-vector bundles which says that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ν
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j(\nu)
            is not orientable.
          %h2#2K-theory 2K-theory of bimonoidal categories
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mo ⊕
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (R, \oplus, \otimes, 0,1, c_{\oplus})
            be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bimonoidal+category"} bimonoidal category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorification"} categorified
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rig"} rig
          %p This can be broken down as
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mo ⊕
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (R, \oplus, 0 , c_{\oplus})
                a permutative category, a categorified abelian
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (R , \otimes, 1)
                is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
                %em strict
                monidal in the following;
            %li
              %p a distributivity law.
          %p
            %strong Examples
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo =
                      %mi Core
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = Core
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinSet"} FinSet
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
                of the category of finite sets and morphisms only between sets of the same cardinality.
              %p
                In the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skeleton"} skeleton
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} mathb
                        %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathb{N}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊕
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \oplus
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊗
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes
                is addition and multiplication on
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mo ⊕
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_{\oplus}
                is the evident natural
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                between direct sums of finite sets.
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mo =
                      %mi Core
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V = Core
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
                of the category of finite dim vector spaces, with morphisms only between those of the same dimension.
            %li
              %p …
          %p
            %strong Definition
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            a bimonoidal category, write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Mat
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mat_n(R)
            for the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ×
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \times n
            matrices with entries morphisms in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            structure.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Gl
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gl_n(R)
            be the category of weakly invertible such matrices. This is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Mat
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mat_n(R)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            squares
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Gl
                            %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi R
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↪
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Mat
                            %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi R
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Gl
                            %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi R
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Mat
                            %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi R
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Gl
                            %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Gr
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi R
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Mat
                            %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Gr
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi R
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  Gl_n(R) &amp;\hookrightarrow&amp; Mat_n(R)
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  Gl_n(\pi_0(R))&amp;\to&amp; Mat_n(\pi_0(R))
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  Gl_n(Gr(\pi_0(R)))&amp;\to&amp; Mat_n(Gr(\pi_0(R)))
                  }
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Gr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gr(-)
            denotes
            = succeed "-completion." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+group"} Grothendieck group
          %p
            %strong Definition
            (Baas-Dundas-Rognes, 2004)
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bimonoidal+category"} bimonoidal category
            %strong 2K-theory
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mi Ω
                  %mi B
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi Gl
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{K}(R) :=  \Omega B \coprod_{n \geq 0} | B Gl_n(R) |
          %p
            where the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            is forming
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space"} loop space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is forming classifying space of a category and the inner
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is a flabby version of classifying space of a category.
          %p This can also be written
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi Gl
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo +
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\cdots \simeq \mathbb{Z} \times |B Gl_n(R)|^+
                  \\,.
          %p
            Here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mi q
                  %msub
                    %mi Gl
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_q Gl_n(R)
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+category"} simplicial category
          %p …
          %p
            %strong Theorem
            (Baas-Dundas-Rognes)
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bimonoidal+category"} bimonoidal category
            such that
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                is a
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            %li
              %p
                for all
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in R
                we have that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \oplus (-)
                is
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/faithful+functor"} faithful
          %p
            Then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{K}(R) \simeq K(H R)
            is the ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectrum"} ring spectrum
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H R
          %p
            Notice that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H R
            to be a spectrum we only need the additive structure
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mo ⊕
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (R, \oplus, 0, c_{\oplus})
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊗
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes
            indeed makes this a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectrum"} ring spectrum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
            and Elmendorf-Mandell (2006).
          %p
            %strong Examples
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                For the category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo :
                      %mo =
                      %mi E
                      %mo =
                      %mi Core
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi FinSet
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R := E = Core(FinSet)
                of finite sets as above we have that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi H
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H E
                is the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
            %li
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo :
                      %mo =
                      %mi V
                      %mo =
                      %mi Core
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi FinDimVect
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R := V = Core(FinDimVect)
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+spaces"} complex
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+dimensional+vector+spaces"} finite dimensional vector spaces
                we have
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi H
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H V
                is the complex
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+spectrum"} K-theory spectrum
            %li
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_{\mathbb{R}}
                analogously we get the real K-theory spectrum.
          %p So by the above theorem
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒦
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{K}(E) \simeq K(S) \simeq A(*)
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒦
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ku
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{K}(V) \simeq K(ku)
                ;
            %li
              %p etc.
          %p
            %strong Remarks
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                A. Osono: The equivalence
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒦
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi H
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{K}(R) \simeq K(H R)
                of
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
                = succeed "s;" do
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    infinity loop space
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/infinity+loop+space"} ?
            %li
              %p Application of that:
              %p
                a) for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                a
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectrum"} ring spectrum
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi H
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      E \simeq H R(R)
              %p
                and use the equivalence
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝕂
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi H
                      %mi R
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{K}(R) \simeq K(H R E)
                to understand
                %em arithmetic
                properties of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              %p
                b) Often one knows
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(H(R))
                via calculations. here
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒦
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{K}(R)
                might help to get some deeper understanding.
              %p
                c) Theorem (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Birgit+Richter"}> Birgit Richter
                ): for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                a bimonoidal category with anti-involution, then you get an involution of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒦
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{K}(R)
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/red-shift+conjecture"} red-shift conjecture
          %h2#References References
          %p The original article:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nils+Baas"}> Nils Baas
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ian+Dundas"} Ian Dundas
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Rognes"} John Rognes
              = succeed "," do
                %em Two-vector bundles and forms of elliptic cohomology
              = succeed "," do
                %em Topology, Geometry and Quantum Field Theory
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 308
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0306027"} arXiv:math/0306027
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://www.mn.uio.no/math/personer/vit/rognes/papers/segal60.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511526398"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511526398
          %p
            Their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+spaces"} classifying spaces
            are discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nils+Baas"}> Nils Baas
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ian+Dundas"} Ian Dundas
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Birgit+Richter"} Birgit Richter
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Rognes"} John Rognes
                %em Ring completion of rig categories
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0706.0531"}> arXiv:0706.0531
                )
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (a previous version of this carried the title
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %em Two-vector bundles define a form of elliptic cohomology
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nils+Baas"}> Nils Baas
                , M. Böckstedt,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tore+Kro"} Tore Kro
                %em Two-Categorical Bundles and Their Classifying Spaces
                (2008) (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0612549"}> arXiv:math/0612549
                ), .
          %p Divisibility of the gerbe on the 3-sphere, seen as a 2-vector bundle is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Ausoni"}> Christian Ausoni
              ,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bj%C3%B8rn+Ian+Dundas"} Bjørn Ian Dundas
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Rognes"} John Rognes
              = succeed "," do
                %em Divisibility of the Dirac magnetic monopole as a two-vector bundle over the three-sphere
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://eudml.org/doc/45387"} dml:45387
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.univ-paris13.fr/~ausoni/papers/ADR08.pdf"} pdf
          %p Orientation of BDR 2-vector bundles is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              Thomas Kragh,
              %em Orientations and Connective Structures on 2-vector Bundles
              Mathematica Scandinavica, 113 (2013) no 1, (
              %a{:href => "http://www.mscand.dk/article/view/15482"}> journal
              ), (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0910.0131"}> arXiv:0910.0131
              )
